From 26d365e3528fab6bcc35598b811bac7742ee9b43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: omarchy-m5 <omarchy-m5@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:34:59 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: j714s: expose only PERST# on the AP pin
 controller

The N1 root port's PERST# is pin 80 of the AP pin controller. This tree
described the three pin banks but no kernel ever bound them, because
the driver was only built as a module the boot path does not load: with
the N1 port enabled the PCIe host then deferred forever on reset-gpios.

With the driver built in, restrict what it may touch. Pin 112's
register takes an SError when read on this SoC (J716c finding), so
reserve every AP pin but 80, as t6050-j716c.dts does, and leave the NUB
and AOP banks disabled: nothing uses them and their registers have not
been checked on this board.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s-n1.dtsi | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s-n1.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s-n1.dtsi
index 9d285c29a..c9d54d141 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s-n1.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-j714s-n1.dtsi
@@ -133,3 +133,24 @@ dart_apcie0: iommu@410000000 {
 		status = "disabled";
 	};
 };
+
+/*
+ * PERST# needs the AP pin controller, which this tree described but never
+ * bound (no driver was built in). On this SoC pin 112's register
+ * (0x29c0001c0) takes an SError when read (J716c finding), so only the pin a
+ * node names is exposed: 80, PCIe port 0's PERST# ([ADT] pci-bridge0
+ * function-perst). A reserved line cannot be requested: a node that names
+ * another pin has to open it here.
+ */
+&pinctrl_ap {
+	gpio-reserved-ranges = <0 80>, <81 140>;
+};
+
+/* Nothing here uses the NUB or AOP pin banks, and their registers are unchecked. */
+&pinctrl_nub {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
+
+&pinctrl_aop {
+	status = "disabled";
+};
-- 
